Repro from S11 (TrialViewMapFxSuite "cells without coverage are hatched…").
Setup:
- headless Monocle, 720×440 logical px;
- P17 ret_07, blank display, 1920×1080 screen;
- 64×48 grid with cells x 8–23, y 8–23 missing;
- light theme, dark stage;
- row across the hole at frame y = 16 cells.

Results:
- no legend, scale 1: opaque (warn-soft 251,241,217);
- legend under the trial (canvas fits 720×402), scale 1: ~75% alpha;
- no legend, scale 2: ~75% alpha;
- legend, scale 2: opaque (the committed test).

When it is translucent, every pixel is one of three colours, (226,219,200), (165,142,96) and (129,96,36). These are warn-soft and warn-text at alpha 0.75 over the screen token #9A9A96, so this is not sampling aliasing. Once fixed, the test can go back to scale 1.
